==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*skek-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|schaken}}, from {{inh|en|ang|sċeacan}}, {{m|ang|sċacan|t=to shake}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*skakan}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*skakaną|t=to shake, swing, escape}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*(s)keg-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*(s)kek-|t=to jump, move}}.

Cognate with {{cog|sco|schake}}, {{m|sco|schack|t=to shake}}, {{cog|fy|schaekje|t=to shake}}, {{cog|nl|schaken|t=to elope, make clean, shake}}, {{cog|nds|schaken|t=to move, shift, push, shake}} and {{m|nds|schacken|t=to shake, shock}}, {{cog|non|skaka|t=to shaka}}, {{cog|nn|skaka|t=to shake}}, {{cog|sv|skaka|t=to shake}}, {{cog|da|skage|t=to shake}}, {{cog|nl|schokken|t=to shake, shock}}, {{cog|ru|скака́ть|t=to jump}}. More at {{l|en|shock}}.

